  "resources": {
    "cheatsheet": {
      "title": "Esoteric Computing Studies \u2014 Cheat Sheet",
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Hermetic Principles",
          "items": [
            "Close reading \u2014 the careful reading is structural analogy: patterns at one scale illuminate patterns at another (microcosm/macrocosm). The honest reading asks what the claim meant to its authors and what it does in their system.",
            "Analogy vs identity \u2014 collapsing analogy into identity is how careful metaphysics becomes sloppy mysticism; holding the distinction is the whole critical skill.",
            "Philosophical analysis \u2014 the critical move is neither belief nor dismissal but analysis \u2014 what would follow if it were true, what evidence could bear on it, where it begs the question.",
            "Common trap \u2014 that mind or perception is primary in the account of reality.",
            "Common trap \u2014 that everything in the universe is literally identical.",
            "Common trap \u2014 that the tablet is a recipe for transmuting lead.",
            "Common trap \u2014 that ancient authors understood neuroscience.",
            "The careful reading is structural analogy \u2014 patterns at one scale illuminate patterns at another (microcosm/macrocosm). 'As' signals correspondence, not identity \u2014 the text doesn't claim a planet IS an atom."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Enochian System",
          "items": [
            "Source criticism starts here \u2014 we have Dee's records of Kelley's reports, not direct access to anything else.",
            "Systematicity \u2014 whether one 'uses' it or studies it, the systematicity is the datum: somebody built (or received) a complete machine, not a pile of parts.",
            "System analysis \u2014 fixed sequence + cosmological mapping = a navigable architecture: each Call addresses a specific region of the system's universe, in order.",
            "Transmission reshapes \u2014 the Golden Dawn's Enochian is Dee's material refracted through Victorian magical theory.",
            "Common trap \u2014 it's a constructed script with its own alphabet, delivered as a received system.",
            "Common trap \u2014 tables, squares, and letter-grids function as a notation: positions encode relations, like coordinates or code.",
            "Common trap \u2014 dee channeled everything alone in trance.",
            "Common trap \u2014 it's a naturally evolved language like English.",
            "A \u2014 A complete, internally consistent script appearing in a few years is remarkable whether one attributes it to angels, the unconscious, or fraud \u2014 each hypothesis must explain the systematicity. Linguists note its structures; historians note the delivery meth\u2026"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Cybernetics & Hyperstition",
          "items": [
            "Feedback loops \u2014 hyperstition: a fiction that makes itself real through the feedback loops it triggers \u2014 the bank-run rumor, the self-fulfilling investment thesis, the manifesto that recruits its own movement.",
            "Second-order \u2014 Second-order cybernetics notes that social systems contain their own observers: predictions alter behavior (self-fulfilling or self-defeating prophecies), measurements disturb. It's second-order cybernetics applied to narrative: stories as causal agents.",
            "Reflexivity \u2014 the critical reader asks what the fiction illuminates (reflexivity, anticipation) without mistaking the device for a discovery.",
            "Hyperstition concept \u2014 the concept earns its keep wherever beliefs move markets, politics, or code \u2014 which is to say, everywhere social. The honest use of hyperstition marks this boundary explicitly.",
            "Theory-fiction \u2014 a philosophy collective that treated theory-fiction, jungle music, and cybernetics as one continuous practice \u2014 deliberately dissolving the line between analyzing systems and performing them.",
            "Common trap \u2014 a CCRU-associated motif: time as non-linear, with the future leaking into the present.",
            "Common trap \u2014 that time travel is physically proven.",
            "Common trap \u2014 it includes the observer in the system: the act of observing/modeling changes what's observed.",
            "Common trap \u2014 accept every hyperstitional claim as true.",
            "Second-order \u2014 Second-order cybernetics notes that social systems contain their own observers: predictions alter behavior (self-fulfilling or self-defeating prophecies), measurements disturb. The thermostat is first-order \u2014 observed from outside. The market is second-orde\u2026"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Symbol Systems",
          "items": [
            "Arbitrariness of the sign \u2014 the sign works by social convention, not natural resemblance.",
            "Literacy \u2014 a tiny reusable sign-set collapses the cost of literacy: anyone can learn 26 shapes, so reading stops being a scribal monopoly.",
            "Notation externalizes cognition \u2014 positional numerals, algebraic symbols, and dy/dx turn mental operations into visual manipulations you can perform reliably. Technologies of notation aren't neutral containers; they rewire what their users can think.",
            "Contemporary symbols \u2014 emoji work like rebus pictographs: context-flexible symbols that modulate alphabetic text \u2014 marking tone, softening requests, disambiguating intent.",
            "Common trap \u2014 it democratized literacy: a small set of reusable signs (20-odd letters) can encode any utterance, versus thousands of memorized glyphs.",
            "Common trap \u2014 psychologically: condensing an intention into a symbol gives the mind a handle.",
            "Common trap \u2014 notation is just shorthand with no cognitive role.",
            "Common trap \u2014 emoji function like rebus writing: pictographs carrying flexible, context-dependent meaning.",
            "Nothing about t-r-ee resembles a tree \u2014 Spanish says \u00e1rbol, Japanese says ki. This arbitrariness is what makes language flexible (any meaning can attach to any sound) and what makes translation lossy (conventions differ). Every symbol system \u2014 including code \u2014 inherits this: variable names mean b\u2026"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Critical Reading",
          "items": [
            "Historical semantics is the entry fee for old texts \u2014 check the OED's dated senses, read contemporaries, and never trust a familiar word.",
            "Translation criticism \u2014 source criticism doesn't disprove the teachings' value \u2014 it correctly prices the lineage claim.",
            "Genre decides the reading stance \u2014 a ritual manual's ascent is a visualization protocol; a cosmology's is a truth claim; an allegory's is a moral map.",
            "Source criticism \u2014 compare translations, consult the source term, and treat translator disagreement as information about conceptual mismatch, not noise.",
            "Anachronism is evidence \u2014 the live hypotheses are later interpolation, misdating, or forgery (or a genuinely independent anticipation \u2014 rare, and needing strong proof).",
            "Common trap \u2014 determine the genre first: cosmology, allegory, ritual manual, and polemic each demand different reading stances.",
            "Common trap \u2014 keep sources distinct: map each claim to its source, note agreements and tensions, and let contradictions stand as data.",
            "Common trap \u2014 pick your favorite source and ignore the rest.",
            "Common trap \u2014 pick the translation that sounds best.",
            "Recover period meaning first \u2014 'enthusiasm' then meant divine inspiration, not naive overexcitement. Reading with modern definitions manufactures nonsense the author never wrote."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Esoteric Programming",
          "items": [
            "Control flow \u2014 the program counter gains a direction on a plane: > sends it right, v down, and control flow becomes literal geometry \u2014 loops are circuits, branches are forks in a maze.",
            "Spatial computing \u2014 it exposes how much ordinary programming leans on the hidden convention 'next = down one line.' Befunge makes sequence spatial, and in doing so reveals sequence was always a choice.",
            "Parody is analysis by caricature \u2014 by pushing design tics past the line, INTERCAL maps exactly where the line is.",
            "Naming \u2014 SPL literalizes what good programmers know: naming is casting.",
            "Common trap \u2014 parody as critique: INTERCAL's 'features' (politeness modifiers, line-noise operators) satirize real language design tics by exaggeration.",
            "Common trap \u2014 control flow becomes geometry: the instruction pointer moves on a 2D grid, redirected by arrow commands.",
            "Common trap \u2014 both are precise utterances where exact repetition matters: a mispronounced word or mistyped character breaks the operation.",
            "Common trap \u2014 constraints as engines: Oulipo-style rules and esolang restrictions force invention.",
            "SPL literalizes what good programmers know \u2014 naming is casting. 'Romeo' carrying a value through scenes makes vividly clear that identifiers are roles in a drama of state \u2014 the program is a play, execution a performance. The esolang's joke is a genuine insight: code is read by humans performing it in\u2026"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
