      },
      {
        "term": "Spanish",
        "def": "Nothing about t-r-ee resembles a tree \u2014 Spanish says \u00e1rbol, Japanese says ki. This arbitrariness is what makes language flexible (any meaning can attach to any sound) and what makes translation lossy (conventions differ)."
      },
      {
        "term": "Feedback",
        "def": "Feedback: sense the output, compare to the goal, adjust the input \u2014 the loop that lets systems steer. Wiener's leap was seeing the same loop in machines, organisms, and societies: purposeful behavior without a little homunculus inside, j\u2026"
      },
      {
        "term": "Historical",
        "def": "Historical semantics is the entry fee for old texts \u2014 check the OED's dated senses, read contemporaries, and never trust a familiar word."
      },
      {
        "term": "Golden Dawn",
        "def": "Transmission reshapes: the Golden Dawn's Enochian is Dee's material refracted through Victorian magical theory."
      },
      {
        "term": "Anachronism",
        "def": "Anachronism is evidence: the live hypotheses are later interpolation, misdating, or forgery (or a genuinely independent anticipation \u2014 rare, and needing strong proof)."
      },
      {
        "term": "Transmission",
        "def": "Transmission reshapes: the Golden Dawn's Enochian is Dee's material refracted through Victorian magical theory."
      },
      {
        "term": "Hyperstition",
        "def": "Hyperstition: a fiction that makes itself real through the feedback loops it triggers \u2014 the bank-run rumor, the self-fulfilling investment thesis, the manifesto that recruits its own movement. It's second-order cybernetics applied to nar\u2026"
      },
      {
        "term": "MEANT",
        "def": "The texts' authority for Renaissance readers came largely from their supposed antiquity \u2014 'prisca theologia,' ancient theology. Redating them to the 2nd\u20133rd centuries CE doesn't erase their interest, but it relocates it: from primordial\u2026"
      },
      {
        "term": "PLEASE",
        "def": "COME FROM inverts goto and thereby indicts it \u2014 showing unstructured jumps are absurd from either direction. PLEASE satirizes arbitrary compiler strictness."
      },
      {
        "term": "Japanese",
        "def": "Nothing about t-r-ee resembles a tree \u2014 Spanish says \u00e1rbol, Japanese says ki. This arbitrariness is what makes language flexible (any meaning can attach to any sound) and what makes translation lossy (conventions differ)."
      },
      {
        "term": "Naming",
        "def": "Naming: SPL literalizes what good programmers know: naming is casting."
      },
      {
        "term": "Systematicity",
        "def": "Systematicity: whether one 'uses' it or studies it, the systematicity is the datum: somebody built (or received) a complete machine, not a pile of parts."
      },
      {
        "term": "Close",
        "def": "Close reading: the careful reading is structural analogy: patterns at one scale illuminate patterns at another (microcosm/macrocosm). The honest reading asks what the claim meant to its authors and what it does in their system."
      },
      {
        "term": "Satire",
        "def": "Satire works by exaggeration \u2014 what real tendencies is INTERCAL exaggerating?"
      },
      {
        "term": "Analogy",
        "def": "Analogy vs identity: collapsing analogy into identity is how careful metaphysics becomes sloppy mysticism; holding the distinction is the whole critical skill."
      },
      {
        "term": "Control",
        "def": "Control flow: the program counter gains a direction on a plane: > sends it right, v down, and control flow becomes literal geometry \u2014 loops are circuits, branches are forks in a maze."
      },
      {
        "term": "Literacy",
        "def": "Literacy: a tiny reusable sign-set collapses the cost of literacy: anyone can learn 26 shapes, so reading stops being a scribal monopoly."
      },
      {
        "term": "Aphoristic",
        "def": "Aphoristic form is a technology: compressed, memorable lines designed to be unfolded slowly through commentary, memorization, and meditation. The brevity isn't missing content \u2014 it's the pedagogy."
      }
    ],
